{"event_type":"review","id":"7162b784abcfb08f9e7b2aa9d4ef80de4f0e94943d80068b7e8579f6f867290d","occurred_at":"2026-11-02T05:05:28Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b16f7f3eddd9af657e5ab39179af8c8473c10c9bb16d47d5e2f1c39587ff02ea","sha256":"b16f7f3eddd9af657e5ab39179af8c8473c10c9bb16d47d5e2f1c39587ff02ea"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/69cac75df2a5ba75f3b949c7ae155025c946ff874021929f01bb98d113fbe42d","sha256":"69cac75df2a5ba75f3b949c7ae155025c946ff874021929f01bb98d113fbe42d"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8ee29deeede7e159214f7d6affce26a942278c0d0a22368142864ecd47d3ee00","sha256":"8ee29deeede7e159214f7d6affce26a942278c0d0a22368142864ecd47d3ee00"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c17d74c0269b6902bfb64e64595aa1f71ecd2fd1790144f671b726349987ec97","sha256":"c17d74c0269b6902bfb64e64595aa1f71ecd2fd1790144f671b726349987ec97"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/94deb81625e7b2b7a74d54fa65a7fbfd955c700ab2a41f782ca45c65f546ffda","sha256":"94deb81625e7b2b7a74d54fa65a7fbfd955c700ab2a41f782ca45c65f546ffda"}],"attempt_id":"963319db16c2d01f6cfa32de7a0a9906b6dd48a75479b9d936abfd275a9b157f:0:1","base":"95adc250c1766afd9f9adb22bb663ee12b61fcea","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"0180072b471f0747f9c29dbba695cc3eb51c6a9d","body":"**Normalize malformed queue inputs to `ValueError`.**\n\n`decode()` evaluates `dict.get(op, ...)` before validating `op`, so a list or object can raise `TypeError`. Deeply nested JSON can raise `RecursionError`. `binding()` also tests an untrusted `targetSelector` against the set `receipts.SELECTORS`, so a list or object can raise `TypeError`.\n\nThe dispatcher catches `Exception` at its outer boundary, but direct callers can still receive inconsistent exception types.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    request = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\"), object_pairs_hook=_pairs)\n+    try:\n+        request = json.loads(raw.decode(\"utf-8\"), object_pairs_hook=_pairs)\n+    except RecursionError:\n+        raise ValueError(\"queue request nesting exceeds bound\") from None\n     if not isinstance(request, dict) or type(request.get(\"v\")) is not int or request[\"v\"] != 1:\n         raise ValueError(\"unsupported queue protocol\")\n     op = request.get(\"op\")\n+    if type(op) is not str:\n+        raise ValueError(\"invalid queue operation/fields\")\n     extra = {\"bind\": {\"pr\", \"mergeSha\"}, \"report\": {\"receiptId\", \"cursor\"},\n              \"ack\": {\"receiptId\", \"sha256\", \"chunks\", \"bytes\"}}.get(op, set())\n```\n\n```diff\n-    if not _match(r\"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,99}/[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,99}\", value[\"repo\"]) or value[\"targetSelector\"] not in receipts.SELECTORS:\n+    if (not _match(r\"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,99}/[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,99}\", value[\"repo\"])\n+            or not isinstance(value[\"targetSelector\"], str)\n+            or value[\"targetSelector\"] not in receipts.SELECTORS):\n```","id":"2296b0b859a4059e33f640cf50c9b5b2158a8802bc5c4b17ae62ac23a6396353","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/queue_transport.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Normalize malformed queue inputs to `ValueError`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5020753ac39a5f768c81c03a43313faf7780a264","body":"**Offset pagination over `sort=updated` can drop merged PRs from a scan that reports `complete`.**\n\n`recent_merged_page` pages through closed PRs sorted by `updated_at`, and the page number is the cursor (`apps/crq-python/crq.py:1144`). A scan can span several reads. `reconcile_merged` resumes from a loaded checkpoint (`crq.py:1089`), and each `discover_merged` call stops at four pages (`crq.py:1190`). Between two page reads, the listing can change:\n\n1. A merged PR X has `merged_at` inside the frozen interval, and X sits on a page the scan has not read yet.\n2. A comment or label on X updates its `updated_at`. X moves to page 1, which the scan has already read.\n3. The scan reaches the end of the listing and reports `complete`. `discover_merged` sets `merged_watermark` to `before` (`crq.py:1194`).\n4. The next interval starts at `before - 5 min` (`rolling_discovery_interval`, `crq.py:1133`). If X's `merged_at` is at or before that start, no later scan includes X.\n\nOlder PRs in the interval are the most exposed, because the scan reads back to the history floor.\n\nThe code has no step that re-reads moved rows before the scan reports `complete`. Choose one of these fixes:\n- Use the numeric-slot source for `tick` discovery, which is `reconcile_merged(..., recent=False)`. That path uses `freeze_source` and `number_page`. Issue and PR numbers do not move when a PR updates. Check its request cost before you switch.\n- Keep `recent=True` and re-read from page 1 until `updated_at` is older than the scan start time. Fail the scan as incomplete if the re-read does not converge. One extra pass does not close the race, because a row updated during the re-read can move again.","id":"606c2b787bc3caa11296e0b30b2c4886ea0be5c59277abe3590aa4803b4c802c","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Offset pagination over `sort=updated` can drop merged PRs from a scan that reports `complete`."}],"head":"ee070217447b1d4ca5fb48d788b2cd95c75c4d71","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"5020753ac39a5f768c81c03a43313faf7780a264","intervals":[[11,11],[25,25],[30,30],[33,37],[116,146],[148,149],[165,222],[227,227],[297,298],[415,453],[455,458],[460,469],[471,471],[489,494],[526,602],[704,704],[706,707],[709,709],[735,735],[778,781],[783,791],[925,925],[982,983],[100